#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# permutation_sign

#% text
# `permutation_sign(p)`: 1 for an even permutation, -1 for an odd one (p cycles or an image list)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is a permutation in cycles or a list of images of 1, ..., n.

#% item
# A permutation is even when it has an even number of cycles of even length.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
permutation_sign(cycles([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5]]))
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
permutation_sign([3, 1, 2])
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
permutation_sign(cycles([]))
#% output
#= 1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `permutation_cycle_type`, `alternating_group`
